WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.830
While we wait with bated breath for Netflix
to release news about an eventual Stranger

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.590
Things season four, we've collected the information
we already do have, along with a few interesting

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:12.620
theories, as a way to help make the uncertainty
a little more manageable.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.430
The announcement for Stranger Things' fourth
season came in the form of a short video teaser,

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:21.710
which displays the words "Stranger Things
4" in the show's glowing red title font, as

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.189
its eerie synthesized theme music swells.

00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:28.480
That is, before the dark vines of the Upside
Down rise to ominously choke out the red light

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.180
of the words.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.080
The teaser finishes with a card announcing,
"We're not in Hawkins anymore," which could

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.880
either refer to the Upside Down, or to the
expanded geography of the show.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.860
After all, the Byers family did move away
from the Indiana town at the end of season

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.860
3, which also teased a new, Soviet Union-based
subplot.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.000
In the season 3 finale, police chief Jim Hopper
finds himself dangerously close to the machine

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.070
the Soviet scientists constructed to open
a gate to the Upside Down, right as Joyce

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.620
Byers prepares to destroy it.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:59.520
Both Hopper and Joyce realize what she has
to do, and seconds later, the machine explodes,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.820
killing the nearby Russian scientists and
presumably Hopper as well.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.540
But we never see Hopper's body, either during
or after the explosion.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.080
When Joyce goes to look at what's left of
the machine, there's no trace of him.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.840
Perhaps he jumped through the gate at the
last second and is now trapped in the Upside

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:23.340
Down.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:24.980
Or maybe he emerged somewhere else.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.039
In a season 3 finale post-credits scene, we
get a glimpse of a facility in Russia and

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.640
a closed door sealing off a character referred
to only as "the American."

00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:36.979
There are a number of candidates for who the
American is, but in an interview with SlashFilm,

00:01:36.979 --> 00:01:41.140
David Harbour, who plays Sheriff Hopper, indicated
that he does, in fact, believe his character

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.540
is alive, all the way off in the USSR.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:47.759
While Hopper is probably the strongest contender,
other theories have proposed that it could

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:53.360
actually be Dr. Brenner, Billy Hargrove, Murray
Bauman, or even a character we haven't yet

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:53.860
met.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.260
Whoever it is, we'll find out for sure in
season 4.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:01.219
Series co-creator Ross Duffer told Entertainment
Weekly that the identity of the American,

00:02:01.219 --> 00:02:04.859
along with the truth of what the Russians
are doing with the demogorgon, will play a,

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.840
quote, "huge role" in season 4.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.140
The same end-credits scene that teases the
American also introduces a fascinating and

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:15.620
terrifying new development to the world of
Stranger Things: the Soviets have a demogorgon.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.830
In the scene, Russian guards toss a terrified
prisoner into a large metal cage before turning

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:23.959
a crank that releases the beast from its pen,
indicating that they've been keeping at least

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.560
one of the creatures in captivity.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.780
This may explain why the Soviets were working
to open gates to the Upside Down in the first

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:30.280
place.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.180
Perhaps they've been collecting demogorgons,
although for what purpose we can't be sure.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:37.879
The fact that they're feeding them humans,
however, suggests that their motivations are

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:38.880
far from benevolent.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:44.159
With the first season of Stranger Things taking
place in the winter of 1983, the second in

00:02:44.159 --> 00:02:49.209
the fall of 1984, and the third in the summer
of 1985, some fans are speculating that the

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:52.120
fourth season will be set in the spring of
1986.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:56.160
If it is, there's a possibility that the fourth
season will somehow tie into the Chernobyl

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:00.020
nuclear disaster, which occurred on April
26, 1986.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:04.000
The Soviet presence in season 3 lends weight
to the theory that we might be spending more

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.260
time in the USSR in season 4.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:10.360
While incorporating a deadly real-life disaster
into a series about alternate dimensions and

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:14.660
monsters feels like precarious ground, there's
one disturbing theory that takes the Chernobyl

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:19.520
speculation a step further, proposing that
it may actually be Eleven who causes the disaster.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:23.220
Either she'll get her powers back and somehow
cause the nuclear reaction herself, or her

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:26.820
battle with the creatures from the Upside
Down will have catastrophic repercussions,

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.180
which will then be swept under the rug with
a story about a nuclear accident.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.780
"Mysterious deaths, government cover ups,
a bizarre chemical leak.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.411
Is it all linked?

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:38.920
All a vast conspiracy?"

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:43.500
Although Dr. Brenner appeared to have died
at the end of season 1, season 2 revealed

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.520
that he survived the bloody finale and is
still out there, somewhere.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.180
"I can help.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:50.620
I can help you find him."

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:55.180
However, Brenner was nowhere to be found in
season 3, leading fans to wonder what's become

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:55.680
of him.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.280
Since Eleven ended season 3 without her powers,
some fans speculate that Dr. Brenner will

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.440
be the one to help her get her abilities back.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.560
"Shhh, you're sick.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.093
You're sick, but I'm going to make you better.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.160
I'm going to take you back home, where I can
make you well again."

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.980
After all, he's the person who guided her
through developing and honing them in the

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.980
first place, so it makes a twisted sort of
sense that he might be the key to her regaining

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:18.480
them.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:23.180
After being possessed by the Mind Flayer for
most of season 3, Billy was finally able to

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:26.760
resist the creature's mind control long enough
to protect Eleven from being flayed.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:31.440
Unfortunately, he was no match for the giant,
multi-armed monster, and was impaled multiple

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.940
times before dying in his stepsister Max's
arms.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:38.030
However, one theory suggests that Billy may
have survived after all, and may yet return

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:38.940
in season 4.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.600
Not only did Billy manage to hold on to his
own body, unlike most of the Mind Flayer's

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:46.610
victims who melted before merging into a single
monster, but we don't see what becomes of

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.440
him after Max goes to his side at the mall.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.320
It's possible that someone could have arrived
to save his life just in the nick of time.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.380
If Billy is alive, he could be the mysterious
American in Russia.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.020
While this seems like a long shot, it makes
sense that Russians would take an interest

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:02.720
in Billy, since their research would surely
benefit from studying one of the few people

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:06.160
who has been taken over by the Mind Flayer
and maybe lived to tell the tale.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:11.520
The 1985 film Back to the Future was a major
pop culture touchstone for season 3, playing

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:16.030
in the movie theater that the Stranger Things
kids frequent and even providing amusing conversation

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:19.140
fodder for a drugged-with-truth-serum Steve
Harrington and Robin.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.540
"What's happening?"

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:26.419
"I have no idea."

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.979
But perhaps the appearance of a movie about
a time-traveling teenager was about more than

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:35.660
providing a nostalgic Easter egg for the audience,
and was actually hinting at future storylines.

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:40.280
In a show that has already normalized concepts
like alternate dimensions, monsters, possession,

00:05:40.289 --> 00:05:44.699
and telekinesis, time travel doesn't feel
entirely outside of the realm of possibility

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:45.480
for season 4.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:49.600
It could make a lot of sense, given that time
travel was part of the original concept for

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:50.240
the show.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:51.420
"The future.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:52.980
That's where you're going."

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:56.640
And we still understand very little about
the properties of the Upside Down, or the

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.420
extent of Eleven's powers.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:02.419
It wouldn't be totally unreasonable to discover
that characters may be able to move back and

00:06:02.419 --> 00:06:06.699
forth through time, possibly even changing
some of the darker events of the past.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.960
This opens up a world of possibilities for
the show.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.600
Maybe we could witness the return of Barb
or Bob Newby.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:15.800
And, if Hopper and Billy really are dead,
time travel may be the perfect solution to

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:16.860
go back and see them again.

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:21.400
While official casting information hasn't
yet been released, it's a safe bet to assume

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.639
that all of the surviving main characters
will be coming back for season 4.

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:28.860
The Byers family may have moved, but considering
they took Eleven, a central character and

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:32.500
the only one with superpowers, with them,
it seems unlikely that they wouldn't return.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:36.540
In fact, the Byers' move could be a way to
open the storytelling possibilities for the

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.040
series.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.860
Matt Duffer told Entertainment Weekly:

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:41.949
"I think the biggest thing that’s going
to happen is it’s going to open up a little

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:45.349
bit...in terms of allowing plotlines into
areas outside of Hawkins.”

00:06:45.349 --> 00:06:49.069
Although the Duffers didn't get into detail
regarding which outside areas they meant,

00:06:49.069 --> 00:06:52.260
we can take a couple of educated guesses based
on season 3.

00:06:52.409 --> 00:06:56.840
The first is obviously the Soviet Union, where
the third season both began and ended.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:00.220
Perhaps whatever strange things happen in
the fourth season will take the Hawkins crew

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:01.420
on an adventure abroad.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:06.180
Another strong possibility is the as-yet undisclosed
town that the Byers crew now calls home.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:10.819
Although Joyce talked a lot in season 3 about
her family's need for a fresh start, the location

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:14.940
of their home was conspicuously omitted from
any of the dialogue, leaving every possibility

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:15.440
open.

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:20.060
Wherever season 4 takes us, Ross Duffer says
we should expect it to feel, very different

00:07:20.069 --> 00:07:21.160
from what's come before.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.300
He told Entertainment Weekly:

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:25.340
"But I think that's the right thing to do
and I think it'll be exciting."

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:30.139
Before the Byers family and Eleven move away,
Mike and Eleven confirm their plans to see

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:30.900
each other again.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:35.270
Mike says he's received the okay from his
parents to go stay with the Byers' over Thanksgiving

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:38.880
and suggests that perhaps Will and Eleven
might return to Hawkins for Christmas.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.200
"Did you talk to your mom?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.060
About Thanksgiving?"

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:42.840
"Yeah.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.180
Yeah, yeah, yeah, I got the okay.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:44.860
I'll be there."

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:49.760
While either one of these suggestions could
hint at the timeframe for season 4, Thanksgiving

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:54.009
seems the more likely option, since each season
has centered around a holiday, and the show

00:07:54.009 --> 00:07:55.760
already did Christmas in season 1.

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:59.670
If Mike's Thanksgiving trip to the Byers'
new home is indeed the catalyst for season

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:03.260
4, we can probably expect the season to drop
around November 2020.

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:07.419
That would allow 16 months between the release
dates of seasons three and four, which seems

00:08:07.419 --> 00:08:10.620
about right given the amount of time between
the existing seasons.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:14.510
15 months between the releases of seasons
one and two, and 21 months between two and

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:15.000
three.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:19.500
Although news of an official renewal didn't
come until a few months after season 3, that

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.260
didn't stop the Duffer brothers and executive
producer Shawn Levy from looking ahead.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:26.620
While everyone involved in the production
of the show seemed to be on the same page

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:30.900
as far as taking the story beyond season 3,
just how far they plan on going seems to still

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.000
be a little up in the air.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:35.120
In an interview with Collider ahead of season
3, Levy said:

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.789
"Season Four is definitely happening.

00:08:36.789 --> 00:08:40.960
There’s very much the possibility of a season
beyond that one, that’s currently undecided."

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:44.670
Meanwhile, the Duffers have said that while
they see the show lasting at least four seasons,

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.240
they don't want to go on for too long.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.870
Ross Duffer told Entertainment Weekly:

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.700
"Like we’re going to stretch credibility.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.020
It wasn’t intended to be a seven-season
thing."

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:56.610
That would indicate that the lifespan of Stranger
Things is somewhere between four and six seasons,

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.890
with something on the lower side feeling the
most likely.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:02.950
But whether season 4 proves to be its last,
or it continues on for another season or two

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:06.950
past that, it sounds as though the Duffers
are intent on ending the show on its own terms,

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:08.920
rather than allowing it to overstay its welcome.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:13.620
Nearly a year before season 3 appeared on
Netflix, rumors started circulating that the

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:17.320
third season of Stranger Things would be the
last for the Duffer brothers as showrunners.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.260
While it was thought that the creative duo
might still stay on with the show in some

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:23.660
capacity, their input into its overall direction
would be greatly reduced.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:27.480
This came as a blow to fans of the show, since
the Duffers were the ones who created the

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:29.300
world of Stranger Things in the first place.

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:32.520
Losing the Duffers at this point would've
robbed the audience of the opportunity to

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:35.220
see the conclusion the original creators had
envisioned.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:39.380
However, Netflix quashed that rumor as definitively
as the time Hopper stomped on a skittering

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:41.580
piece of Mind Flayer at the Starcourt Mall.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:48.140
The streaming service tweeted in February
2018:

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:49.920
"Don't drop your Eggos.

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:53.940
Rumors that the Duffer Bros are leaving Stranger
Things after season 3 are false."

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:57.931
Rest assured, whenever Stranger Things does
eventually draw to a close, it will be with

00:09:57.940 --> 00:09:59.160
the Duffers at the helm.

